  data:  # 6d56
    kind: work_item  # 6d56
    title: "go: a net.Dial*/Listen* connection on a unix-family network stamps net_stream (network); an AF_UNIX socket is process-local (pipe -> ipc) -- the Go twin of WI-baran"  # 6d56
    status: todo_hard  # 6d56
    priority: 3  # 6d56
    parent:  # 6d56
    tags:  # 6d56
    - io_boundary  # 6d56
    - taint  # 6d56
    - go  # 6d56
    isbefore: []  # 6d56
    duplicate_of: []  # 6d56
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 6d56
    pr_ref:  # 6d56
    description: "FOUND 2026-09-28 reading back INV-totar's A/B. go.py stamps every net.Dial / net.DialTimeout / net.Listen connection io_target_kind=net_stream, so a Unix-domain socket is a network crossing. podman pkg/machine/shim/claim_darwin.go: con, _ := net.DialTimeout(\"unix\", helperSock, ...); fmt.Fprintln(con, \"GO\") -> io-boundaries net_send, taint zone network. It is a process-local socket: pipe -> ipc_send / ipc is the exact answer.\n\nThis is the Go twin of WI-baran (c sys/socket send*/recv*: the descriptor's FAMILY decides, AF_UNIX -> pipe). The first argument of net.Dial* / net.Listen* is the network name as a string literal in the common case (\"unix\", \"unixgram\", \"unixpacket\" -> pipe; \"tcp*\"/\"udp*\"/\"ip*\" -> net_stream; a variable abstains).\n\nFIX SHAPE: read the literal network argument where the connection is bound; stamp pipe for the unix family. Both consumers (io-boundaries and taint, now wired by INV-totar) follow the stamp. Size first: count net.Dial*/Listen* by network literal on the Go cohort."  # 6d56
    fields: {}  # 6d56
- op: discuss  # 46f6
  at: '2026-10-03T12:12:25Z'  # 46f6
  by: agent  # 46f6
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 46f6
  clock: 2  # 46f6
  nonce: 46f6  # 46f6
  message: "WORK DONE 2026-10-03 (concurrent run, local branch, not pushed). Branch jgstern-agent/fix/potog, commit 09b93f0bb4 on origin/dev e8d9e89ca4. go.py only; go.yaml NOT touched.\n\nMECHANISM = WI-baran's (family fixed at creation decides pipe vs net_stream; accept follows the listener one binding back), in Go spelling: _go_socket_family_kind reads net.Dial/DialTimeout/Listen/ListenPacket's first argument when it is a string literal (\"unix\"/\"unixgram\"/\"unixpacket\" -> pipe; \"tcp*\"/\"udp*\"/\"ip*\", protocol suffix ignored -> net_stream) or the constructor's name (DialUnix/ListenUnix/ListenUnixgram -> pipe; DialTCP/DialUDP/ListenTCP/ListenUDP -> net_stream). _go_classify_handle_text asks it for every connection producer; _go_target_kind_from_expression follows ln.Accept() to ln's last binding. net.DialUnix( joined the connection producers; (\"net\",\"UnixConn\") is a typed pipe. Existing dual rows + _WRITE/_READ_TARGET_KIND_BOUNDARY do the rest, so both consumers follow.\n\nNON-LITERAL NETWORK (variable, named constant, URL scheme): keeps today's net_stream. Stated, not guessed: Go's stamp IS the row selection, so abstaining would move fmt.Fprint* to logging and io.WriteString to fs_write -- the same reason C's rows abstain_to net_*. Same for an unknown literal (\"fd\"), another package's Dial (regex-anchored on `net.`), a listener with no visible binding or a tls.NewListener binding. Pinned by tests.\n\nEVIDENCE. Live fixture (net.DialTimeout(\"unix\") + Fprintln; Dial(\"unixgram\") + io.WriteString; Listen(\"unixpacket\") + Accept + bufio + Fprintln; DialUnix; *net.UnixConn param; tcp/variable controls), io-boundaries before -> after: Fprintln net_send -> ipc_send (unixDial, unixListen), io.WriteString net_send -> ipc_send, bufio.NewReader / Reader.ReadString net_recv -> ipc_recv, DialUnix and UnixConn Fprintln logging -> ipc_send; tcpDial, varDial, tcpListen unchanged net_*. Taint (verify-claims host_secret -> ipc): dev confirmed (0 flows) -> branch VIOLATED at fmt.Fprintln. Tests: test_go_socket_family_origin.py 39 tests (26 red on a stub, 13 controls green both ways), + unix case in test_go_taint_sink_follows_the_writer.py. Board smart-test: 10002 passed, 3 xfailed, changed source at 100% coverage. Mutation (tcp -> pipe, fallback -> pipe) in a scratch copy moves the tcp/variable controls, so they can fail.\n\nA/B, io-boundaries --format json, arm A = git archive of e8d9e89ca4, arm B = branch, fresh cache per arm, code-under-test path printed per arm; 21 Go repos (every <200MB repo with a unix-literal site: podman containerd moby linuxkit vpnkit gvisor-tap-vsock container-libs docker-cli buildkit buildah istio spire swarmkit distribution alertmanager gin opa trivy vault kserve ingress-nginx) + the fixture as control (7 moved, as above). COVERED 21 of 21, all rc=0. MOVED 5, REMOVED 0, ADDED 0, total_io_edges identical per repo; every moved row read back as a unix socket: podman claim_darwin.go Fprintln net_send->ipc_send (DialTimeout \"unix\"); containerd pkg/shim/util_unix.go hybridVsockDialer Fprintln net_send->ipc_send (DialTimeout \"unix\"); vpnkit dialer_darwin.go io.WriteString net_send->ipc_send (Dial \"unix\"); container-libs slirp4netns.go Fprintf net_send->ipc_send (Dial \"unix\"); linuxkit service/logging.go bufio.Reader.ReadString fs_read->ipc_recv (DialUnix; before: unstamped fallback, now a real untrusted_input source). NOT covered: cilium (428MB), kubernetes (380MB), test files (io-boundaries default excludes them); taint verdict movement on the corpus not measured (io tagging only).\n\nWHY SO FEW MOVE: a text census over the corpus (non-test) counts 49 unix-literal net.Dial/DialTimeout + 50 net.Listen sites, but the bound connection is mostly passed elsewhere (31) or used through its own methods: x.Write 8, x.Read 3 -- net.Conn.Write/Read are single rows that read no stamp. Filed WI-kalol-vinud-kozog-zakar-kufuh-bunub-lapun-zibap.\n\nALSO FOUND, filed: WI-gajir-hiral-havip-dosan-fapun-jufuk-mahum-hugih (P2) -- on dev, net.Dial(\"tcp\") + fmt.Fprintln(con, secret) confirms the network claim with 0 flows: the content flow is collapsed with net.Dial's resource-naming-only flow and excluded. Pinned in the branch as a strict xfail. NOT changed (WI-baran's connect precedent): the dial/listen call rows themselves.\n\nInstrument + outputs: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/decontend/run_10032026/potog/ (ab_one.sh, ab_cohort.sh, ab_diff.py, ab_compare.out, cohort.log, *.A.json/*.B.json)."  # 46f6
